<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I79b214648501f552f470212dbd2877827cde665a" commit="61e3cfc517100e2c9fe9cd14b2f138f048fa150f" commit_message="umpire: webapps: allow more webapps been registered under /webapps  umpire can support multiple webapps but the handler registered under /resourcemap for the single webapp_resourcemap. In order to allow more webapps, handler should register to /webapps then multiple webapps can be under this common URL. For example, resourcemap would be /webapps/resourcemap .  In order to support legacy client who still access to /resourcemap, the request of /resourcemap will be passed to /webapps/resourcemap via nginx config.  BUG=b:80152439 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I79b214648501f552f470212dbd2877827cde665a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1126585 Commit-Ready: Marco Chen &lt;marcochen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Marco Chen &lt;marcochen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1126585" owner_email="marcochen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/85/1126585/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic1822301d383f9360c1cc26ee4db408f591112be" commit="f91039029a322701761f157338c9c8841ac9082e" commit_message="umpire: webapps: add a new webapp - Download Slots Manager  According to DUT (device under test) info embedded in request header, either it will assign a new UUID to present a unique session if no uuid cookie presented or keep a session alive mapped from the UUID in cookie. On the other hand, one more information - N_PLACE will be returned which indicates whether the DUT gets available download session (N_PLACE: 0) or been put in the queue due to slots are all occupied already (ex: &quot;N_PLACE: 3&quot; shows that two DUTs are waiting for the slot in front of it). In the end, the cookie of drop_slot would indicate that this session is done so the slot can be reclaimed for other session.  BUG=b:80152439 TEST=manually test between DUT and factory server  Change-Id: Ic1822301d383f9360c1cc26ee4db408f591112be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1127080 Commit-Ready: Marco Chen &lt;marcochen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Marco Chen &lt;marcochen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1127080" owner_email="marcochen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="18" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/80/1127080/18" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I804239108060adbd9ee0f9ecff0931b06e1fffb9" commit="573ba6ff55349b2d869a480edb08724185f98d83" commit_message="Remove external module 'enum' and 'logilab'.  External module 'logilab' is no longer used by anyone, while another module 'enum' isn't used in an intense way and could be easily replaced by 'type_utils'. Remove these two modules to minimize our codebase.  BUG=b:112252329 TEST=make smartlint &amp;&amp; make test  Change-Id: I804239108060adbd9ee0f9ecff0931b06e1fffb9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1164142 Commit-Ready: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1164142" owner_email="youcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/42/1164142/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifaafefacdbe6b6f377dca53a1a0578eccc44e7b8" commit="a23f2ca998694412078f24a3831c0b346b0de3ea" commit_message="platform2: Get rid of FilePath::FromUTF8Unsafe stuff  It's safe to assume file paths are UTF-8 on Chrome OS.  Along the way, fix minor lint errors trigerred by the changes:  - Remove (c): Do not use (c) in copyright headers in new files - unsigned long -&gt; ULONG: Use int16/int64/etc, rather than the C type long  The latter is safe because ULONG == unsigned long per clang:   xULONG ss_percent = MapDbmToPercent(signal_strength);   ^~~~~~   ULONG ../../../../../../../usr/include/gobi/types.h:6:28: note: 'ULONG' declared here typedef unsigned long      ULONG;  BUG=chromium:870621 TEST=make sure that the affected packages in platform2 build: % cros_workon --board=$BOARD start arc-obb-mounter gobi-cromo-plugin power_manager virtual-file-provider % ./build_packages  CQ-DEPEND=CL:1166273  Change-Id: Ifaafefacdbe6b6f377dca53a1a0578eccc44e7b8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1166615 Commit-Ready: Satoru Takabayashi &lt;satorux@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Satoru Takabayashi &lt;satorux@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1166615" owner_email="satorux@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/15/1166615/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibb4194ff9af13458f8dfa0ef1c82b93f0956c795" commit="77965558c85dcd4ce921e7d42a1c94e08f70b4c1" commit_message="crash: Add crash_sender_paths.h/cc  This is in preparation for moving more paths and functions using the paths from the shell script. Get() and SetPrefixForTesting() are introduced to make the path-based functions unit-testable. A unit test for IsMock() is added based on the test helpers.  Along the way, fix the #include orders.  BUG=chromium:391887 TEST=Run the unit tests  Change-Id: Ibb4194ff9af13458f8dfa0ef1c82b93f0956c795 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1154785 Commit-Ready: Satoru Takabayas